1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,150
Anaxagoras thought we are the wisest
animals because we have hands.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:10,150
Aristotle turned it round: we have hands
because we are wise.

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:12,525
Robots finally have hands.

4
00:00:12,575 --> 00:00:18,150
Teaching them should be easy, for
repetitive work, and for delicate work.

5
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,553
With Rokoko Smartgloves you just move.

6
00:00:21,603 --> 00:00:27,844
On a real Unitree G1, the gloves drove
both arms and both hands:

7
00:00:27,894 --> 00:00:33,650
two runs of 120 seconds, zero commands
clipped by the safety filter.

8
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,936
But gloves cannot feel.

9
00:00:35,986 --> 00:00:39,954
The operator feels the egg; the robot does
not.

10
00:00:40,004 --> 00:00:46,650
A confident fist on the human side is a
crushed egg on the robot side.

11
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:49,483
So the robot looks first.

12
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:52,750
A head camera asks two model families.

13
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,483
NVIDIA Nemotron answers in a median 0.22
seconds.

14
00:00:56,533 --> 00:01:02,550
Google Gemma, and PaliGemma on our own
Verda GPU, give the second key.

15
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:08,150
Fragile first: if one credible model says
egg, it is an egg.

16
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:13,014
The object sets how far the fingers may
close.

17
00:01:13,064 --> 00:01:17,862
A stress ball closes fully only when both
families agree.

18
00:01:17,912 --> 00:01:23,195
In simulation, same egg, same fist: with
the cap, held intact.

19
00:01:23,245 --> 00:01:24,650
Without it, broken.

20
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:29,928
On our fifty photos, the vote got fifty of
fifty,

21
00:01:29,978 --> 00:01:35,183
and every disagreement between Nemotron
and Gemma was one model's mistake.

22
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:40,439
One person, one place, one day: a start,
not a proof.

23
00:01:40,489 --> 00:01:46,650
Confidence never told right from wrong, so
no single model unlocks full closure.

24
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:49,650
Repetitive work: the glove teaches.

25
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:52,150
Delicate work: the camera protects.

26
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:57,150
And every demonstration comes out labelled
for the next robot.

27
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,650
Now it's easy.

